<title>LATVIA: MOST SHARES IN MADONA BLOCKED BEFORE MEETING.</title>
<headline>MOST SHARES IN MADONA BLOCKED BEFORE MEETING.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central depository said on Wednesday that most shares in fur company Madona-AB were blocked ahead of a June 28 shareholder meeting.</p>
<p>The depository said in a statement that of 351,981 shares in issue, some 343,659 shares were blocked.</p>
<p>Most shares, 51.48 percent, belong to the Evma company, indviduals Vladimir Falilejev and Ilze Erina have 10.45 percent and 6.33 percent each while the privatisation agency holds 5.27 percent.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
